  id: S16_11
  era: "Section 16 \xB7 Mughal Empire \xB7 1526 \u2013 1857"
  title: Religion under the Mughals
  text: Akbar held debates in the Ibadat Khana and promoted tolerance; the Din-i-Ilahi was a small spiritual circle around him. Later emperors differed, and Aurangzeb followed a stricter orthodoxy. Many Mughals patronised shrines of several faiths.
